---
title: Hirundinidae
---
# Hirundinidae

Hirundinidae is the swallow and martin family, slender aerial insectivores with
long wings and a short, wide bill. Many species build a nest of mud pellets
carried one at a time and stuck fast to a vertical wall or a beam; others dig a
burrow, and a few nest in cavities lined with grass and feathers. Nothing in the
family suspends its nest from a branch. See [[barn-swallow]].
